statement:
Let \(G\) be a hypothetical Erdős #595 witness with a stable partition
having finite edge fibers. Then one of the following occurs:
1. a finite acyclic support-pruning core exists;
2. a finite unicyclic support or fixed-point core exists;
3. a finite minimal incoherence core of cycle rank at least two exists;
4. the entire realized-type hypergraph has a coherent section and is an
   exact uncountably chromatic Berge-\(C_3\)-free compression of \(G\).

Enumerate inclusion-minimal finite \(K_4\)-free fiber-coherence cores whose
incidence cycle rank is at least two. After exact tree absorption, record:
1. a minimum variable feedback set;
2. the restricted forest certificate for every feedback assignment;
3. the cycle-space relations induced between feedback variables;
4. whether one cycle alone already has a fixed-point obstruction;
5. whether incoherence first appears only through interaction of two or
   more individually coherent cycles.
Determine whether genuinely mixed multicycle cores exist and classify the
smallest one.
